This product bundles Xiph.Org Foundation software, vendored under
ios/Vendor/ and used to decode Ogg Vorbis and Ogg Opus, neither of which
Apple's Core Audio supports:

  libogg 1.3.5     — ios/Vendor/ogg,    see ios/Vendor/ogg/COPYING
  libvorbis 1.3.7  — ios/Vendor/vorbis, see ios/Vendor/vorbis/COPYING
  libopus 1.4      — ios/Vendor/opus,   see ios/Vendor/opus/COPYING
  libopusfile 0.12 — ios/Vendor/opus/opusfile,
                     see ios/Vendor/opus/COPYING-opusfile

libogg and libvorbis are Copyright (c) 2002-2020 Xiph.org Foundation.
libopus is Copyright 2001-2011 Xiph.Org, Skype Limited, Octasic, Jean-Marc
Valin, Timothy B. Terriberry, CSIRO, Gregory Maxwell, Mark Borgerding and Erik
de Castro Lopo. libopusfile is Copyright (c) 1994-2013 Xiph.Org Foundation and
contributors. All four are licensed under the 3-clause BSD licence, reproduced
in the COPYING files above.

The sources are unmodified. Only a subset is included: the decoders, plus the
Vorbis encoder, which the test suite uses to generate a real Vorbis bitstream
rather than depending on an external tool. Xiph's own build system files and the
standalone tools carrying their own main() are omitted.

libopusfile is vendored inside ios/Vendor/opus rather than beside it because it
is built as one library with libopus and shares its include root; its licence is
separate and is the COPYING-opusfile named above.
